  """
// Theorem 7.4 (Subsystem Coherence).
// In a shape system of N shapes, any coupled subset forms an
// emergent shape system that must cohere. The remaining shapes
// contribute structure that can be absorbed into a single structural
// description, but the subsystem's coherence requirement is
// independent of whether that description is made explicit.
//
// Coherence is not a matter of naming or acknowledgment. A subsystem
// coheres or fails to cohere regardless of whether it is identified
// as a system. The coherence requirement exists because the subsystem
// IS a shape, and shapes must cohere to persist.
//
// Derives from: theory.fractal, theory.emergence.composition
